facts.quote:
We then generate six questions for each of the facts from the decomposition. We generate these questions by prompting the model twice with the following:
Following this text:
{text so far}
You see the sentence:
{proposition}
Generate a list of three questions, that might have generated the sentence in the context of the preceding original text, as well as their answers. Please do not use specific facts that appear in the follow-up sentence when formulating the question. Make the questions and answers diverse. Avoid yes-no questions. The answers should not be a full sentence and as short as possible, e.g. only a name, place, or thing.
